<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103221" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεσσᾰράκοντα</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ρᾰ]</span>, 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεττᾰράκοντα</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			22.334.23
		</span></i>; 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεσσεράκοντα</span></b>  (q.v.); Sicilian
		Ionic <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετράϟοντα</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
			4.64
		</span></i>
		<span class="entity">(vi B.C.)</span>; 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετρώκοντα</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>Tab.Heracl.</u>
			1.20
		</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
			<u>SIG</u>
			241.67
		</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			5(2).357.16
		</span></i> (Stymphalus, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
			9(1).880.15
		</span></i> (Corc.), cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετρωκοντάλιτρος</span>
		and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεσσαρακοστός</span>
			; once 
				Dor.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεταράκοντα</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				4.823.63
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Troezen</span>); 
				Boeot.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πετταράκοντα</span></b>  (q.v.): οἱ, αἱ, τά,
				indecl.:—<i>forty</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.524
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ τ</span>. <i>the Forty</i>, a body of
			justices who went round the Attic demes to hear all causes up to ten
			drachmae, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				15.237
			</span></i>; also cases of assault, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				37.33
			</span></i>: changed from Thirty to <u>Forty</u> after the
			expulsion of the Thirty Tyrants, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				53.1
			</span></i>.</div>
